From 5899113b4a06c0548c0446a448ebe94ef3ff5ce8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:49:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(videos): stop generated slugs ending in a doubled hyphen,
 name the Cullinan review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two things made /our-videos/m3m-cullinan-noida-is-the-32000sqft-4-bhk-actually-worth-it--D9cK37IEPH8
the URL for the first Reviews-channel upload.

The doubled hyphen was a bug. getVideoSlug truncated the slugified title to
60 characters AFTER trimming trailing hyphens, so a cut that landed on a
hyphen kept it, and appending "-<id>" produced "…worth-it--D9cK37IEPH8".
Truncation now happens first, falls back to the last complete word so a slug
never ends mid-word, and trims again before the id is added.

The id on the end is not a bug — it is how the watch page resolves an upload
that has no hand-written entry yet, live from the API, instead of 404ing.
The fix for the ugly URL is to give the video an entry, so this adds one:
slug m3m-cullinan-noida-4-bhk-review, with the description and content
written from the video. getVideoBySlug already matches an id-suffixed slug
against a curated youtubeId, so the old URL now 308s to the clean one and
only the clean one gets indexed.

getVideoSlug moves to src/lib/videoSlug.ts (re-exported from youtube.ts so
importers are unchanged) because youtube.ts's Next-specific fetch options
cannot compile under ts-node, and scripts/verify-video-slug.ts needs to run
the real function.

